      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "We’ve been asking for more transparency for years now. They’ve got the discord, medium, dev stream and now the community forum posts. None of these are being utilised in a way that provides reasonable detailed information on the development. There is only ever information whenever something becomes publicly available. \nAs a more recent example of poor communication not development related, there were multiple events that happened recently within vrchat that we’re never announced. Until the new UI supports announcements you really need to put the effort into letting people know when something gets a dedicated row for an event, what it’s for and roughly how long it will remain available.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-01-13T21:24:01.178Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I'm someone who absolutely loves getting an inside look at what goes into a game's development. There's so much happening that we don't see and/or never hear about; the only insight we get is the small patches being pushed here and there, and the bare-bones community updates (which also should be fleshed out a lot more). As a reference, the last recorded dev stream was April 22, 2020. I'd love to see a lot more transparency with VRChat's development!",
